subsection.subsection:
In an application for an adjustment or deferral described in Subsection (1), the applicant shall include a statement setting forth the following:
a description of the property;
the value of the property for the current year;
the amount of delinquent taxes, interest, and penalties;
for an adjustment, the amount proposed to be paid; or
for a deferral, the amount proposed to be deferred; and
any other information required by the county legislative body.

section.subsection:
Within 10 days after the day on which a county legislative body grants an adjustment or deferral, the county legislative body shall cause the adjustment or deferral to be posted in the county where the property involved is located.  The publication shall contain:

the name of the applicant;
the parcel, serial, or account number of the property;
the value of the property for the current year;
the sum of the delinquent taxes, interest, and penalty due; and
the adjusted amount paid or deferred.
